1.4 \textbar{} Goals of this study
\par
1. To assess the performance of CNNs for classifying images into
\par
different animal species, empty images, and human or vehicle
\par
images from four camera trap projects.
\par
2. To assess how an established technique called ``transfer-learning''
\par
can help train models for projects with a low number of (human
\par
classified) images which are generally more challenging to accu-
\par
rately model.
\par
3. To implement and evaluate a trained model in the context of a
\par
live citizen science project on Zooniverse to observe its applica-
\par
bility under real-world conditions and test for improvements in
\par
classification efficiency.
