2.2 \textbar{} Citizen science and image classification
\par
Each capture event was annotated by multiple citizen scientists
\par
using the Zooniverse platform. The research teams for each project
\par
configured how many annotations per capture event they required
\par
before it was considered finished (retired)---balancing classification
\par
quality and time to process the whole dataset. The retirement limits
\par
were class specific and often dynamically adjusted based on volun-
\par
teer consensus. For example, SW collected annotations for a given
\par
capture event until seven volunteers agreed on one species with a
\par
cap at 15 annotations. Overall, the retirement limits ranged between
