\par
The researchers built project-\- specific workflows by selecting
\par
different options for tasks to be done by the citizen scientists. For
\par
the SS, EE, and SW datasets the researchers used the ``survey task''
\par
workflow in which the capture events were shown to citizen scien-
\par
tists along with all possible classifications to choose from. CC used a
\par
novel ``cascade filtering'' procedure to improve the retirement speed
\par
of empty and vehicle images. In this latter approach, images were
\par
initially processed through the ``Empty or Not'' workflow asking vol-
\par
unteers to identify empty images. Nonempty images were subse-
\par
