\par
model required each image to be associated with one unique class,
\par
we aggregated multiple annotations. We used the plurality algorithm
\par
as described in Swanson et al. (2015) to achieve consistent labelling
\par
across all projects. The algorithm first determines the number of dis-
\par
tinct species that each image contains. If the majority of volunteers
\par
identified more than one species in a capture event we excluded it
\par
from the study due to the additional complexity involved in model-
\par
