\par
3.2 \textbar{} Confidence thresholding
\par
With confidence thresholding, predictions were ignored if the
\par
model assigned low probabilities and thus indicated uncertainty.
\par
Figure 6 shows the effect of confidence thresholding on prediction
\par
accuracy and dataset coverage for different thresholds on the EE
\par
species model trained from scratch (see all figures in the Supporting
\par
Information). Accuracy for all models increased with increasing
\par
thresholds while reducing coverage. However, even if we set the
\par
threshold to 99\%, which resulted in accuracies between 96.7\% and
\par
98.9\%, coverage remained at 76\%--86.5\% for the species models.
\par
The empty models reached slightly higher accuracies (97.5\%--99.4\%)
\par
and coverage (73.7\%--94.7\%). Noteworthy are the high accuracies
\par
of the empty models for CC (99.4\%) and EE (98.9\%), as well as ac-
\par
curacies over 99\% for several frequent species across all datasets
\par
(ignoring statistically insignificant accuracies for rare species).
\par
