\par
to treat an individual meta-analysis as itself a single study or witness report, perhaps
\par
a very reliable one if it is based on considerable data from multiple experiments (but
\par
see Stegenga 2011 for doubts about the reliability of meta-analyses). The latter route
\par
is attractive because in practice there are many meta-analyses at hand that account
\par
