8. DISCUSSION
\par
Fire danger and risk research has evolved from the development of qualitative indices, to de-
\par
terministic models of fire characteristics, to stochastic models of fire characteristics. It is an on-
\par
going challenge to integrate these models and approaches in probabilistic, quantitative hazard
\par
and risk models. Improving prediction of daily wildfire dynamics is critical for proactive rather
\par
thanreactivefiremanagementdecisionmaking.Effectivepredictionfordecisionmakingrequires
