\par
study also suggests GA is very helpful to overcome the premature
\par
convergence and high sensitivity to initial conditions of NARX.
\par
As a data-driven model, the RNN uses mathematical equations with
\par
many parameters to replace the complex kinetic processes of physical
\par
models, and this can be seen as a parameterization of the reservoir
\par
operation (Chaves and Kojiri, 2007). The RNN models in this study
\par
adopt several constraints with physical signi cance (e.g., water balance
\par
equation, hydraulic constrains for reservoir storage and dam release,
\par
etc.) and thus the results still obey the basic physical laws and boundary
\par
conditions. Since actual reservoir operation is a continuous optimiza-
\par
tion process, the feedback from the downstream is also important to
\par
improve the reservoir operation for satisfying the water management
\par
requirement in the downstream. The RNN model training based on the
\par
historical input and output data can extract the previous reservoir op-
\par
erators' experience, and therefore, the simulation results of the RNN
\par
model can also be a good reference for the current reservoir operators.
\par
