DISCUSSION
\par
A need for variable, disaggregated benchmarks
\par
We present a statistical method to estimate best-on-
\par
offer (benchmark) reference states using a large number
\par
of vegetation survey plots distributed along broad cli-
\par
matic, biogeographical, and disturbance gradients. We
\par
demonstrated estimation of native species richness and
\par
cover benchmarks that accounted for spatial variation
\par
