\par
mean-dose-intensity and time-on-treatment(ToT) parameters attributed most to the
\par
decision uncertainty.LTTACC provided the smallest PSUB and the most robust NMB
\par
estimates under parametric uncertainty.For scenarios on increased regorafenib ToT
\par
or mean-dose-intensity,LTACC again provided acceptable cost-effectiveness out-
\par
comes,whereas for scenarios on decreased regorafenib PFS\&OS, only PBRSA resulted
\par
in plausible ICER values. In some scenarios(e.g.exploring uncertainty on the pro-
\par
gressed disease resource utilization),none of the MEAs resulted in acceptable cost-
\par
