5.Conclusions
\par
Thisstudydeterminedriskfactorsforpreventingfloodand
\par
draining waterlogging in the urban subways through
\par
methods, including investigation, consultation, discussion,
\par
negotiation, and reference to other literatures. In addition,
\par
the listofinfluencefactors for riskevaluationofthe urban
\par
subway was formed. These can be applied to more subway
\par
constructions, and we need to make appropriate adjust-
\par
ments according to the difference of each subway.We
\par
attempted to estimate weights by using the optimal com-
\par
binationweightingmethodbasedonthesubjectiveAHPand
\par
objectiveentropyweightmethod.Inthisway,wecanreduce
\par
errors between the determined weight and the possible
\par
weight of the indexes so that evaluation results are more
\par
realisticandreasonable.Thismethodcanalsobeappliedto
\par
other research fields.
\par
This study established the fuzzy synthetic evaluation
\par
modelforwaterloggingpreventionintheconstructionand
\par
operating periods of the subway station in the city. The
\par
model was applied and validated to be effective in Wen-
\par
jiachangMetroDepotinphaseIofChengduMetroLine4.
\par
The evaluation results coincided with the actual situation.
\par
The model in the study provides a new idea for evaluating
\par
waterlogging risks in urban subway stations, and these re-
\par
sultscanofferimportantinformationforlocalgovernment
\par
to strengthen management on waterlogging risks.
\par
We try to provide a new risk evaluation method for
\par
security experts, architecture design engineer, construction
\par
risk management engineer, government, or other relevant
\par
person, but for the constraints, this method cannot be
\par
verified comprehensively through more actual projects.
\par
Next,furtherresearchwillbecarriedoutthroughthewhole
\par
life cycle of subway projects, not just the construction and
\par
operation periods. We hope this model is widely and
\par
practically applied, and we can achieve further research
\par
resultsandprovidemorereferenceformoreriskassessment
\par
participants.
