\par
variable for computational purposes to reflect the uncertainty in Assumption ii. Note that the linear
\par
uncertain variable is optional since some common uncertain variables such as zigzag uncertain variable
\par
can be applied. Since the causes of travel time uncertainties are unrelated (i.e., the carriers are engaging in
\par
different transportation stages), it is reasonable to assume that the uncertain components are independent.
\par
In Assumption iii, this time-based incentive contract has been used in practice to induce the subcontractors
\par
to increase their effort levels and complete their tasks earlier as proposed by Weitzman [41] and hasEntropy 2019, 21, 161 7 of 20
\par
been used by many researchers and practitioners, see Holmstrom and Milgrom [42]. In Assumption iv,
\par
a quadratic cost function is made not only for expositional convenience but also in accordance with the
\par
practical fact, which has been used in Yang et al. [39] and Tang et al. [43]. Assumption v is reasonable,
\par
because the WRR intermodal transport is a time-limit system for the delivery. That is, the reduction of
\par
delivery time by WRR intermodal transportation will lead to a reduction in financing costs, simply because
\par
the interest payment period will be made shorter after the delivery time is shorter.
