3 Framework of coordinated forecast
\par
system for agricultural means supply
\par
chain
\par
The coordinated forecast on agricultural means supply
\par
chain is comprised of four stages: demand analysis stage,
\par
forecast method implementation stage, forecast effect
\par
evaluation stage and forecast scheme selection stage
\par
(Fig. 1).
\par
3.1 Demand analysis stage
\par
Before forecast, the manufacturers, distributors and retail-
\par
ers on supply chain need to share information (storage
\par
information, production information and marketing infor-
\par
mation in enterprises, market competition information and
\par
policy information out of enterprises etc.) relying on
\par
information technology. At the same time, considering the
\par
goal of supply chain management, analyze the goal of
\par
forecasting demand of market in details to determine
\par
forecast method and forecast means.
\par
3.2 Forecast method implementation stage
\par
The first step is to form a team of coordinated forecast and
\par
its members shall be workers of several departments of
\par
above enterprises, especially the workers of production
\par
department, sale department and logistics department. In
\par
the next step, based on the information collected, jointly
\par
determine the quantitative and qualitative forecast method.
\par
Quantitative forecast method shall combine qualitative
\par
forecast method. Finally, forecast based on historical data,
\par
trend of demand and exceptional cases.
\par
3.3 Forecast effect evaluation stage
\par
In this stage, performance evaluation standards must be
\par
clear to evaluate the accuracy and timeliness of forecast.
\par
The evaluation standards shall be closely related to target
\par
of supply chain. In one aspect, the result of forecast shall be
\par
scientifically evaluated to guarantee the applicability of
\par
forecast method and precision of forecast result. The
\par
forecast method applicable to characters of supply chain
\par
shall be constantly explored and innovated. And base of
\par
forecast methods shall be updated. In another aspect, the
\par
coordination among enterprises and workers in the process
\par
of forecast shall be evaluated to decrease internal friction
