5.2 Forecast result of model and error analysis
\par
Assess performance of the model and compare the forecast
\par
precision of combined forecast model, GM(1,1) \& BP
\par
neural network model and ARMA model. Forecast preci-
\par
sion is the degree of fitting between forecast value of
\par
forecast model and historical actual value. It is used to
\par
evaluate the fitting degree of forecast model. Common
\par
evaluation indexes include the absolute value of absolute
\par
error (AE), mean square error (MSE), mean absolute error
\par
(MAE) and mean absolute percentage error (MAPE).
\par
In Tables 2 and 3, if grey forecast method is indepen-
\par
dently used, only long-term trend can be reflected and the
\par
influence of periodical fluctuation factors on sales volume
\par
cannot be reflected. In comparison, if BP neural network
\par
forecast or ARMA forecast is independently used, error is
\par
much smaller but it is larger than that of combined forecast.
\par
Overall, the precision of combined forecast model is higher
\par
than that of the other three in evaluation of MSE, MAE or
\par
MAPE. Therefore, combined forecast model is very
\par
applicable to research the forecast on agricultural means
\par
sale that is influenced by long-term trend factor and peri-
\par
odical factor.
\par
6 Conclusions
\par
The parts of supply chain of agricultural means link with
\par
each another. The coordinated cooperation of members of
\par
supply chain and scientific forecast method are both
\par
123Cluster Computing (2019) 22:S6621--S6632 S6631
\par
needed. Through comparing the forecast precision of
\par
duplicate combined forecast model, GM(1,1) \& BP neural
\par
network model and ARMA model, it is found that every
\par
forecast has its prominent superiority. However, it is
\par
unavoidable to encounter some abnormal information.
\par
GM(1,1) can well fit future development trend of time
\par
series but its precision of forecast on periodical fluctuation
\par
factors is low. BP neural network has ideal effect of fore-
\par
casting periodical fluctuation factors but it ignores some
\par
loud noise. ARMA can test randomness, stability and
\par
seasonality of time series but the method requires time
\par
series to be stable. Therefore, to raise forecast precision,
\par
the superiority of different forecast models shall be com-
\par
bined. The combined forecast method is especially appli-
\par
cable to forecasting the complex demand of agricultural
\par
means.
