\textbf{6.4 Expected lifetime costs}
\par
Cost-optimum maintenance planning and decision-making under uncertainty have to be performed
\par
with the aid of a probabilistic theoretical framework, which can quantify and assess the benefits and
\par
costs of future maintenance actions, taking the various sources of uncertainties affecting fatigue crack
\par
growth and inspection quality into account. Based on this framework, different maintenance strategies
\par
can be compared in a consistent way before they are implemented in order to select the most
\par
financially-efficient strategy.
\par
The probabilistic framework uses life cycle analysis and risk assessment to formulate the expected
\par
