The main sources of uncertainties associated with crack growth modelling originate from uncertainties
\par
in the initial crack size {$a$}0, the crack growth rate {$C$} and calculation of the stress range ∆{$\sigma$}. Meaningful
\par
statistical data on {$a$}0 is difficult to obtain for specific application due to measuring and sampling
\par
