\par
cost-based approaches are more pronounced. Monte Carlo simulations are carried out to calculate
\par
the probabilities and reliability indexes, with 5 \texttimes{} 106 samples for each variable. It is checked that a
\par
larger number of samples do not lead to much change in the results. An exhaustive search algorithm
\par
is used to obtain the optimal maintenance strategies. A restriction is applied that an inspection can
\par
only be carried out either at the beginning or in the mid of every year. The restriction reduces the
